TITLE: Weekly U.S. Equities Macro Outlook (Sep 21–Sep 25):

TEXT:
Sep 21 (Monday)
Nasdaq -100 and S&P Dow Jones quarterly rebalances take effect before the open; SpaceX ’s weight rises from about 1.28% to 2.82%. Per the source outlooks, S&P 100 adds Palo Alto , Arista , Sandisk and Dell ; S&P 500 adds Bloom Energy and Illumina ; passive rebalancing may stir related tech names;
2027 FOMC voter and Chicago Fed President Goolsbee speaks (18:30);
He Lifeng’s U.S. trade delegation continues talks through the 23rd; Beijing and Washington remain in contact on a possible leaders’ meeting this year; Trump delivers a GOP fundraising keynote in New York;
Sep 22 (Tuesday)
★★★★ The 81st U.N. General Assembly high-level week opens; Trump is due to meet Gulf leaders on a postwar plan for Iran and says he is close to a “big decision” on whether to escalate strikes;
New York Fed President Williams (22:05) and Fed Vice Chair Jefferson (22:20) speak at a U.S. Treasury market conference; Richmond Fed President Barkin speaks (01:00 Beijing time Wednesday / 13:00 ET Tuesday); Treasury auctions $69 billion of 2-year notes;
U.S. releases ADP weekly employment change for the week ended Sep 5 (20:15) and the September Richmond Fed manufacturing index (22:00);
AutoZone ( AZO ) and Thor Industries ( THO ) report before the open;
Qualcomm Snapdragon Summit opens, with the TSMC 2nm Snapdragon 8 Elite Gen6 expected;
new Mac mini and Mac Studio go on sale;
Sep 23 (Wednesday)
★★★★ U.S. releases September S&P Global flash manufacturing and services PMIs (21:45), a post-hike read on growth momentum; EIA crude inventories for the week ended Sep 18 also out (22:30);
Iran’s president Pezeshkian is expected to address the U.N.; Treasury auctions $70 billion of 5-year notes;
Meta Connect 2026 opens, with XR hardware, VR headsets and new smart glasses in focus;
Cintas ( CTAS ), Paychex ( PAYX ), General Mills ( GIS ) and Manchester United ( MANU ) report before the open;
Sep 24 (Thursday)
U.S. releases initial jobless claims for the week ended Sep 19 (20:30) and August new home sales, annualized (22:00);
A cluster of Fed speakers: Williams fireside chat (16:10), Barkin (20:00), Hammack opening remarks (20:50), Paulson at a fintech conference (22:10);
Treasury auctions $44 billion of 7-year notes; with the 10-year yield hovering near 5%, bid demand will test appetite for higher rates;
★★★ BlackBerry ( BB ) reports before the open; Costco (COST) reports after the close;
Sep 25 (Friday)
U.S. releases August durable goods orders, month-over-month (20:30), plus the final September University of Michigan consumer sentiment and 1-year inflation expectations (22:00);
New York Fed President Williams speaks (17:15);
Qualcomm Snapdragon Summit wraps, with focus on the 2nm flagship chip launch and follow-through
*This week’s core U.S. equity themes center on China-U.S. trade talks and Trump’s Iran decision, Fed officials’ signals on the hiking path, the Nasdaq rebalance and SpaceX weight increase, Costco and other consumer earnings, and the Qualcomm/Meta industry events; market volatility is expected to rise
